        "before": "The printed statements use \\[\\bigoplus_{g\\ge2}W_0H_c^{2g}(\\mathcal M_g;\\mathbb Q)\\simeq\\mathfrak{grt}_1,\n \\qquad\n \\mathfrak{grt}_1\\lhook\\joinrel\\longrightarrow\n       \\bigoplus_{g\\ge2}H_{4g-6}(\\operatorname{HMod}_g;\\mathbb Q).\\] For the standard completed \\(\\mathfrak{grt}_1\\) used in the cited theorem, these cannot hold literally. Willwacher distinguishes complete product gradings from direct-sum gradings and defines \\(\\mathfrak{grt}_1\\) by Lie series in the completed free Lie algebra [Retained latex: \\cite[pp.~3, 21]{will}]. The comparison in [Retained latex: \\cite[p.~11, (2.4.2)]{cgp}] likewise uses the algebraic dual of a direct sum.",
